            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What isn't to love! Adjust cooking time for the size of your Asparagus. About 10 minutes was good for mine. Enjoy!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Ann McCann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really don’t like nonstick sprays because they contain additional chemicals and they just contribute waste. So I put the spears in a long pan and very gently drizzled garlic, flavored olive oil over the top of the spears and then tossed them with tongs. Then I placed them on parchment on a jelly roll pan and sprinkled the top with freshly grated Parmesan. (Please do not use pre-shredded cheese; it contains starches that keep the cheese from sticking together, but the starches also prevent the cheese from melting.) I roast, then test. Parmesan is fairly salty. So if I think it needs additional salt, I sprinkle sea salt over the hot asparagus. It’s simple and easy. The right ingredients really matter.",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-20T22:35:14.814Z"
          },
          {
